manual.craftonica.page.19=CURRICULUM 0.4||Use /craftonica lesson list.||Start with:|/craftonica lesson start ID||Check any network block with:|/craftonica lesson check x y z
manual.craftonica.page.20=CLOSED CIRCUIT||ID: closed-circuit||Build Source - Switch - 220 ohms - GND.||Close the switch. Measure 21.739 mA in switch and resistor.
manual.craftonica.page.21=CHALLENGE 1||I = 5 / (220 + 10).||Pass the check. Open the switch and compare: current requires a complete path to GND.
manual.craftonica.page.22=OHM'S LAW||ID: ohm-led-220||Build Source - Switch - 220 ohms - LED - GND.||Anode toward source; close the switch.
manual.craftonica.page.23=CHALLENGE 2||Measure 12.987 mA.||(5 - 2) / (10 + 220 + 1).||Rearrange with wires: the verifier checks quantities, not coordinates.
manual.craftonica.page.24=POLARITY||ID: led-polarity||Build Source - 220 ohms - reversed LED - GND.||Current should stay near zero.
manual.craftonica.page.25=CHALLENGE 3||Obtain POLARITY_INCORRECT.||Then rotate the LED with the wrench and confirm the warning clears and current returns.
manual.craftonica.page.26=SERIES||ID: series-resistors||Build Source - 220 ohms - 220 ohms - GND.||In series, the same current crosses both resistors.
manual.craftonica.page.27=CHALLENGE 4||Measure 11.111 mA in each resistor.||I = 5 / (10 + 220 + 220).||Every resistor branch must pass.
manual.craftonica.page.28=PARALLEL||ID: parallel-resistors||Make two 220 ohm paths between source output and GND.||They share the same two nodes.
manual.craftonica.page.29=CHALLENGE 5||Measure 20.833 mA in each resistor.||The source supplies about 41.667 mA.||Both branches must pass together.
manual.craftonica.page.30=DIAGNOSIS||ID: diagnose-short||Build Source - Wire - GND on a disposable bench.||Obtain SHORT_CIRCUIT, check, then dismantle. Add 220 ohms to fix it.
manual.craftonica.page.31=ROBOBOARD||The programmable board stores only verified firmware and bounded checkpoints.||Execution state belongs to the server.
manual.craftonica.page.32=BOARD STATUS||The built-in D13 light can show firmware output.||Fault state disables execution.||Electrical access uses physical RoboPorts.
manual.craftonica.page.33=ROBOPORT||Use the Configurator on the RoboBoard and then on each RoboPort.||The clicked face connects to the circuit. Use it again to select D0-D13, A0-A5, 5 V or ground.||Terminals may be up to 64 blocks from the board.
manual.craftonica.page.34=ANALOG INPUT||A0-A5 use AVR pins 14-19 internally.||Connect the sensor positive terminal to the RoboPort and its negative terminal to board ground.||The firmware receives an integer sample from 0 to 5,000,000 microvolts.
manual.craftonica.page.35=OUTPUT AND PWM||Set pinMode to OUTPUT and connect a buzzer or motor between the pin and ground.||digitalWrite supplies 0 or 5 V. analogWrite uses the 0-255 DC average on recognized PWM pins.
manual.craftonica.page.36=1.0 LIMITS||The buzzer and motor are resistive loads with visual feedback.||Audio, mechanics, servos, H-bridges, tone() and pulseIn() are not simulated in this version.
manual.craftonica.page.37=SKETCH EDITOR||Right-click the RoboBoard to open its fixed Sketch.ino.||No arbitrary files or host paths are available. Source is limited to 32 KiB.
manual.craftonica.page.38=SHORTCUTS||Ctrl+S compiles.|F5 starts or stops.|F6 switches Editor/Serial.|Ctrl+L clears only the local Serial view.|Esc closes.
manual.craftonica.page.39=SAFE EXECUTION||Compilation and AVR execution run in a limited server sandbox.||Only verified firmware can be installed. The server owns revision and runtime state.
manual.craftonica.page.40=SERIAL TX ONLY||The Serial tab shows only bytes transmitted by the sketch.||History is limited to 8 KiB; offsets and truncation are shown. There is no RX input.
