manual.craftonica.page.15=PROTECTION||The source uses a 5 V Thevenin model with 10 ohms internal resistance.||The breaker opens on the next tick above 100 mA or 0.5 W.||The open state is saved in the world.
manual.craftonica.page.17=POTENTIOMETER||Terminal A, the top wiper and terminal B form two resistive branches.||Click to increase 10%; sneak to decrease.||The course is limited from 0 to 100% and never creates zero resistance.
manual.craftonica.page.18=DIVIDER||Connect A and B to source and ground to make a divider.||Wiper voltage follows the position and branch sum remains 10 kohm.||The multimeter reports ambiguous readings when more than one local branch exists.
manual.craftonica.page.16=RESET||Right-click an open breaker to reset it.||Fix the short before resetting: the nodal result is observed again on the next tick.
